SUMMARY:Strange Stories: Beyond the Ordinary
DESCRIPTION:Fiction goes where real life simply cannot. \nThis panel discussion on fantasy in fiction brings together three authors whose books visit disgruntled demons\, aliens\, and face-burning parties. What becomes possible when fiction stops obeying the rules of the world as we know it? \nThe writers will talk about building alternate worlds\, complete with domes and minarets\, and about the pull of a single what-if that drives such tales. Where facts and fiction vie over the bizarre\, these stories leave everyday routine behind to find the creases and crevices the naked eye misses. Through magic realism\, science fiction\, and futuristic scenarios\, readers and writers meet in new territory. \nVenue: Seminar Halls\n\n\nThe Many Worlds of Fantasy in Fiction\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSctbz-QoMTEOZGoUC_nPO-0qfDFBkJ8-2u3uXQ1y_Qexr0iKg/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Speakers*: Shinie Antony\, Anil Menon\, Lavanya Lakshminarayan\, Arundhati Ghosh\n*Event Categories*: Books\, Fiction
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/strange-stories-beyond-the-ordinary/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Books,Fiction
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Thumbnail_SOS-1.jpg
