SUMMARY:Dekh Tamasha
DESCRIPTION:This storytelling and musical performance blends raw emotion and poetic lyricism with an unflinching look at life’s deeper questions. Inspired by the poet saints Kabir\, Bulleh Shah\, and Lalon Fakir\, the songs and stories invite listeners to pause and look inwards. What does it mean to love in a way that surrenders and questions in equal measure? \nThe Aahvaan Project began in 2016 as a personal search for a philosophy that was equal parts liberating and fulfilling. Today\, it carries the idea of Nirgun love into an intimate setting with personal stories and favourite songs collected over the years.  \nSupported by:\n \nVenue: Library\n\n\nMusical Storytelling by The Aahvaan Project\nRSVPs closed. Thank you for your interest.\n*Performers*: Vedi\, Sumant Balakrishnan\, Makrand Sanon\n*Event Categories*: Music\, Performing Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/dekh-tamasha/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Music,Performing Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Thumbnail-3.jpg
