SUMMARY:Broken o el Necropoder
DESCRIPTION:No life should go unmourned\, and no violence be left unanswered. \nThis multimedia performance looks at femicide in Mexico through the memory and funerary rituals of an Indigenous Oaxacan woman\, who leads the audience to the house of death to demand justice for her sisters. Soil\, flowers\, and candles become part of the staging as the piece pays homage\, in the Oaxacan tradition\, to every body without mourners. Who answers for the dead when no one has come to grieve them? \nDrawing on necropolitics\, the concept developed by Achille Mbembe\, the work begins with a femicide in 2017 and the protest march that followed at the National Autonomous University of Mexico. A site-specific intervention\, it adapts to each space and keeps the audience close\, so no two nights are alike. Songs\, Indigenous languages\, floral offerings\, and ceremonial mezcal turn grief into a sacred act of defiance. \nThis production won Best Actress and Best Set Design at the Hermandades International Festival (2019)\, and is a part of an international tour through France\, Switzerland\, Spain and Mexico (2026). \nCredits:\nPlaywright\, Director & Performer: Darling Lucas\nSet & Lighting Design: Leticia Olvera\nMultimedia Design: Yoatzin Balbuena\nOriginal Music: Yunani Uscanga\nExecutive Producer: Hermana Menor Producciones \nIn collaboration with: \n \nSupported by: \n \nVenue: Gallery\n\n\nA Funeral for Every Unmourned Body\nFor Ages 18+\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdqLVbnDeycZRihOUr4lzPYrYEFhGIJTWzYRSE91JQWbc7Syg/viewform?usp=dialog)\n*Performer*: Darling Lucas\n*Event Categories*: Performing Arts\, Theatre
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/broken-o-el-necropoder/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Performing Arts,Theatre
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Thumbnail_BOEN.jpg
END:VEVENT
