SUMMARY:The Quiet Storm
DESCRIPTION:This classical piano recital travels through Russian\, Polish\, and German Romanticism. The performance moves from the intricate counterpoint of Taneyev\, through the deeply personal and poetic world of Chopin\, to the extraordinary emotional landscape of Schumann\, contrasting intimacy and intensity along the way. Is there beauty to be found within the storms the human spirit endures? \nThe evening opens in Moscow with Sergei Taneyev\, teacher of Rachmaninov and Scriabin. His Prelude and Fugue\, written in memory of his lifelong nurse\, travels from grief to fierce resolve. Next comes Poland and Chopin\, where the storm grows still: two Nocturnes of quiet beauty\, then a Scherzo full of wit\, play\, and sudden flashes of fire. The journey ends in Germany with Robert Schumann\, whose music never rests. His moods change from moment to moment\, torn between passion and dream\, struggle and tenderness. \n \n  \nIn collaboration with:\n \nSupported by:\n    \nAccess contact information for Furtados here. \nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nTaneyev. Chopin. Schumann.\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScm9x6ortUodwBtFC6bk2Wvyzcj_mGMchjrjVs6jqopNYom6g/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Performer*: Rhys Concessao\n*Event Categories*: Music\, Performing Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/the-quiet-storm/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Music,Performing Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Thumbnail_TQS.jpg
END:VEVENT
